# Chaos: missile trails and arcs (O230; client/BASE.md "0147"; src/client/chaosmissile.h (new, pure), missile.h/.cpp,
# luafunctions_client.cpp, mods/client_settings/classes/dataset.lua, options/graphics.otui; after 0001-0146).
# Missile::draw stays the stock single draw. With the option `missileTrails` (default on) and a shot of 2 tiles or more:
#  * Trail: the same missile frame is queued 3 more times at the path fractions f - k * 0.05 (k = 1..3, oldest first, so the
#    missile is on top) with opacities 0.50, 0.32, 0.18 (chaos::missile::trailOpacity). The opacity is DrawQueue::setOpacity
#    over the items queued since the copy started: it only changes their colour (no draw condition, no cache flush). A copy
#    that would lie before the start of the path is left out, so a missile that just left has none. The copies carry no light.
#  * Arc: a missile whose id is in the arc list is lifted by 4 * h * f * (1 - f) pixels (0 at both ends, h in the middle);
#    h = min(14, 1.6 * tiles) pixels of a 32 px sprite, scaled by the sprite size. The trail copies follow the same arc. Missiles
#    outside the list (spell missiles) stay on the straight line. The list is Lua's: game_visualfx sends the stock ids of arrows,
#    bolts, spears and stones with Missile.addArcId, one call per id, like the spell light colours of 0127.
#  * Missile.setTrails(bool) / isTrails() / clearArcIds() / addArcId(id) (static). setTrails is off in the engine, so an engine
#    without the module draws exactly the stock call. With the option off the draw is that stock statement and nothing else.
#  * Not done: the exact angle of single-direction missiles (setRotation is a draw condition; capping it at about 8 and
#    knowing which art has one direction needs the dat, not done blind).
#  * dataset.lua: option `missileTrails` (default on); its apply tells game_visualfx (`onOption('missileTrails', value)`).
#  * options/graphics.otui: one checkbox "Trails and arcs on missiles" under "Smooth health bars"; the visual effects panel
#    grows from 314 to 333 px (one row is 19 px).
